# Probe #12 — DAPM widget + WCD register state during a live silent PCM stream
# Transcribed verbatim from the Hermes background-process completion capture
# (session proc_17e22dfbd4fc, exit 0). Script: /tmp/ear-dapm-v12.sh,
# as-run sha256 db3e8730f5bd7c6ebd6a2ada9842496fff828a1b444ed9fdf33f363aff5989c0
# (not committed; superseded by docs/tools/* and this capture).
#
# Timing: executed BEFORE the K2 hot-swap experiment, on stock kernel/module.
# This is therefore hard evidence that with reset-default K2 = 0x80:
#   - the entire EAR DAPM graph powers On during playback, and
#   - the analog bias / RX supplies / EAR PA registers are all enabled,
# yet the earpiece was physically silent (consistent user reports across v5/v6).
